   "titulo": "The imperative",
   "texto": [
    "In many instructions, the Norwegian imperative ends in consonant: **vaske → vask**, **skrelle → skrell** and **skjære → skjær**.",
    "**Vask** can also be a noun («Sink»); here it is a verb because it gives an instruction. **Rør** also means «tubo», but in the recipe it is «remove»."
